Boston has no great heritage for not  only technology but specifically for  technology related to kind of business  to business and infrastructure  stackdriver was founded in Boston  Massachusetts we founded the company in  2012 it's been really exciting to watch  stackdriver grow and evolve now  deploying stackdriver  across Google infrastructure and taking  advantage of all these exciting Google  technologies  it was beyond anything that we could  have expected only two years  hi I'm Dan Belcher I'm the lead product  manager for operations on the Google  cloud team prior I was one of the  founders of stackdriver  when we started stackdriver we really  didn't have a specific product in mind  instead we were really interested in the  growth of the public cloud and what we  did is we reached out to hundreds of  customers that were running applications  in the cloud and asked them what their  pain points were what we found is that a  lot of customers had disparate tools for  monitoring the cloud platform their  systems their application uptime and so  forth and it was really difficult for  them to not only manage those systems  but to look across those systems to you  know identify it and troubleshoot those  issues and so when we built stackdriver  we built one service that brought all  those capabilities you know together  stack drivers of performance and  availability monitoring for public cloud  infrastructure so you connect us to your  cloud infrastructure either on Amazon  Web Services or Google cloud platform  and we'll show you everything that's  happening inside your infrastructure we  take on the burden of helping you  visualize and run your application  successfully on the cloud without  stackdriver you've got a set up all  kinds of different tooling logging  monitoring dashboarding and we make it  really powerful and simple and really  easy to get started I think that that  removes a lot of excitement when it  comes to reducing a number of  applications one needs to manage our  system so being able to bring that in  one place has alleviates a lot of  problems for DevOps able to see how the  entire episode turns performing  health-wise and performance we also  provide some great tools that are  industry-leading in terms of being able  to do multi conditional learning so now  that you have all the signals come into  one place you can then tailor alerts to  be very specific to conditions that  you're monitoring or relate to an  incident that you've received in the  past  I think custom metrics are one of the  most interesting parts of stackdriver  as an application developer you know  which metrics are the best indicators of  system health so you don't want to  necessarily wait for system metrics like  CPU or memory usage to rise before you  learn the problem so using custom  metrics you can monitor things that are  specific to your application that gives  you an even earlier indication of a  problem they allow you to react more  quickly because you know which metrics  are important in your system we're also  very excited about some of the advanced  features like anomaly detection and  insights that will bring to this product  so people can actually get proactive  insights from the product rather than  just manually setting up alerts and  looking at incidents I primarily focus  on our logging product and our logging  product really is a tool that we have  built that works at scale and can look  at like large enterprise scale customers  who are sending us like gigabytes per  second scale of logs we give them a  platform to visualize those logs and we  also work with those customers to give  them more analytics capabilities on top  of the data so they can make IP ops  operational business analytical as well  as security related decisions find them  quickly and take action monitoring  alerting incident management logging  together into one place  what start driverís promises is that it  will make it easier more streamlined 